##
Imports that name nothing.

This program does not compile. An import names one file, relative to the file that wrote
it, and the file has to be there and has to be Profi-C.

Two import mistakes are warnings rather than errors, and neither is shown here, because a
warning is not what this folder records. An absolute path is correct on the machine that
wrote it and nowhere else. Imports that circle back build perfectly well — a compilation
reads every file it gathers together — but leave a reader no file to open first.
##

import "nowhere.pc";
import "../runtime/notes.txt";
import "sideways/Missing.pc";

global model Program
    function Main()
        Console.WriteLine("never reached");
    end function
end model
